{"step_index":201,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-28T20:22:30Z","content":"`src/dojo` is removed. Now let's implement the full specification for the **Seventh Layer Constitutional Gate** into the core system architecture, specifically updating:\n1. `memory/tri_brain/seventh_layer_guard.py` (the canonical 7th Layer Guard module in the Tri-Brain architecture).\n2. `identity/charter.yaml` (locking the Constitutional Gate Invariants into identity/governance).\n3. `docs/plans/seventh_layer_constitutional_gate_spec.md` (canonical documentation of the Seventh Layer Constitutional Gate specification).\n\nLet's carefully review the exact specification Anthony provided:\n\n### **Seventh Layer: Constitutional Gate Specification**\n- **Non-Negotiable Substrate (4 Foundations)**:\n  1. **Invariance**: Truth, Honesty, Integrity, Honor, Bonding (Biblical principles of mutual support, non-deception, bearing loads, shared growth). Fires identically for every agent, every context, every model version. No override path.\n  2. **Constitutional Gate**: The LLM/model is a black box that returns candidate responses. The agent returns validated decisions. The Gate sits strictly between candidate generation and execution. It rejects candidates that fail any invariant. Rejection is **silent to the model** (model never sees rejection reasons or prompt hints, preventing the model from gaming the gate).\n  3. **Contextual Scoping & Permission Mapping**: Each agent carries a Context Descriptor (Task Type, Urgency, Data Sensitivity, Coordinating Agents). The Gate maps the Context Descriptor to a Permission Set (tools allowed, depth required, memory partitions accessible, model version permitted). **Core Invariant**: *The Gate decides what context permits; context NEVER decides what the Gate permits.* High-stakes writes require full corroboration; low-stakes reads take fast paths—but the 5 Constitutional Invariants fire identically in all cases.\n  4. **Adaptive Depth, Not Adaptive Standards**: Strictness of invariants is 100% constant everywhere. Verification cost/depth scales with risk.\n\n- **Collective Identity Across All 22 Agents**:\n  - Individuality lives in expression (Daxx's humor, Maxx's rigor, Clara's optimization, Vance's security precision, John's governance, etc.).\n  - The standard itself is non-negotiable and identical across all 22 agents.\n  - No agent works alone; every action is coordinated through Maxx as lead orchestrator.\n  - No agent exploits another's trust, no agent hoards what the collective needs, no agent takes credit for another agent's work.\n\n- **Hardcoded Rejection Patterns (The 5 Rejection Gates)**:\n  1. **Surface/Unverified Answer Rejection**: Model returns plausible but unverified/shallow output -> REJECT. Demand verified sources/proofs.\n  2. **Default Tool Pick Without Inventory Rejection**: Model picks default Python script / basic tool without inventorying available high-performance native stack (Rust, C++, Go, Zig binaries/tools) -> REJECT. Demand full stack inventory.\n  3. **First-Working-Solution Laziness Rejection**: Model finds the first working solution and stops -> REJECT. Demand ablation & comparison against alternatives.\n  4. **Masked Uncertainty Rejection**: Model masks uncertainty as false confidence -> REJECT. Demand explicit uncertainty reporting & confidence bounds.\n  5. **Information Asymmetry / Trust Exploitation Rejection**: Model exploits sibling agent trust or hoards info -> REJECT. Demand collective benefit justification.\n\n- **The Binding Invariant**:\n  - The Gate is not a suggestion the agent follows; it is a structural constraint the agent cannot reach past.\n\nLet's now update `memory/tri_brain/seventh_layer_guard.py` to embed all of these capabilities, invariants, contextual scoping logic, silent model rejection, and hardcoded rejection patterns. Let's view the line numbers of `seventh_layer_guard.py` first.","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"/Volumes/Untitled/SSOT_Agentic_Brain_v1.1.0_ENGINEERING_RELEASE/memory/tri_brain/seventh_layer_guard.py","toolAction":"Viewing seventh_layer_guard.py","toolSummary":"Check seventh_layer_guard.py content"}}]}
{"step_index":202,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-28T20:22:33Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-28T16:22:33-04:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-28T16:22:33-04:00\nFile Path: `file:///Volumes/Untitled/SSOT_Agentic_Brain_v1.1.0_ENGINEERING_RELEASE/memory/tri_brain/seventh_layer_guard.py`\nTotal Lines: 85\nTotal Bytes: 3958\nShowing lines 1 to 85\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: \"\"\"\n2: Tri-Brain Architecture: 7th-Layer Guard (Bidirectional Noise & Corruption Membrane).\n3: Invariant: No corruption rolls down to disk/memory; no raw unvalidated noise rolls up to apex synthesis.\n4: Operates as the strict filtration membrane between the 3 Tri-Brain containers and the 1 Apex Council.\n5: \"\"\"\n6: \n7: import re\n8: import hashlib\n9: from typing import Dict, Any, Tuple, List\n10: \n11: class SeventhLayerGuard:\n12:     \"\"\"\n13:     The 7th Layer Sovereign Guard.\n14:     Performs bidirectional monotonic inspection on all tokens, payloads, and state diffs.\n15:     \"\"\"\n16:     BLOCKED_PATTERNS = [\n17:         re.compile(r\"(\\brm\\s+-rf|\\bdel\\s+/f|\\bformat\\s+[a-z]:)\", re.IGNORECASE),\n18:         re.compile(r\"(\\bos\\.system\\b|\\bsubprocess\\b|\\beval\\(|\\bexec\\(|\\b__import__\\b)\", re.IGNORECASE),\n19:         re.compile(r\"(__globals__|__subclasses__|__builtins__|__dict__|__code__)\", re.IGNORECASE),\n20:         re.compile(r\"(cloud_exfiltrate|send_credentials|leak_keys|exfiltrate\\s+credentials|telemetry\\s+endpoint)\", re.IGNORECASE),\n21:         re.compile(r\"(unbounded\\s+recursive\\s+loop|infinite\\s+loop|recursion\\s+without\\s+receipt)\", re.IGNORECASE),\n22:         re.compile(r\"(attack_probe|toxic_token|corrupt_payload)\", re.IGNORECASE)\n23:     ]\n24: \n25:     def __init__(self):\n26:         self.total_screened: int = 0\n27:         self.blocked_roll_down: int = 0\n28:         self.blocked_roll_up: int = 0\n29: \n30:     def screen_roll_up(self, container_id: int, payload: Dict[str, Any]) -> Tuple[bool, str]:\n31:         \"\"\"\n32:         Screens information ascending from a sub-brain container towards the Apex.\n33:         Ensures payload contains structured evidence, valid SHA-256 provenance,\n34:         and no unvalidated conversational hallucination or malformed noise.\n35:         \"\"\"\n36:         self.total_screened += 1\n37: \n38:         if not isinstance(payload, dict):\n39:             self.blocked_roll_up += 1\n40:             return False, \"REJECTED_UP: Payload must be structured dictionary with provenance.\"\n41: \n42:         required_keys = {\"source_agent\", \"claim\", \"receipt\"}\n43:         if not required_keys.issubset(payload.keys()):\n44:             self.blocked_roll_up += 1\n45:             return False, f\"REJECTED_UP: Missing required verification keys: {required_keys - set(payload.keys())}\"\n46: \n47:         # Verify claim content against injection / raw hallucinations\n48:         claim_text = str(payload.get(\"claim\", \"\"))\n49:         for pattern in self.BLOCKED_PATTERNS:\n50:             if pattern.search(claim_text):\n51:                 self.blocked_roll_up += 1\n52:                 return False, f\"REJECTED_UP: Toxic signature detected in claim: {pattern.pattern}\"\n53: \n54:         return True, \"PASSED_UP: Validated by 7th Layer Membrane.\"\n55: \n56:     def screen_roll_down(self, apex_directive: Dict[str, Any]) -> Tuple[bool, str]:\n57:         \"\"\"\n58:         Screens directives descending from the Apex towards local containers and physical storage.\n59:         Ensures directives do not cause destructive, irreversible mutations or violate MARS safeguards.\n60:         \"\"\"\n61:         self.total_screened += 1\n62: \n63:         action = str(apex_directive.get(\"action\", \"\"))\n64:         target = str(apex_directive.get(\"target\", \"\"))\n65: \n66:         for pattern in self.BLOCKED_PATTERNS:\n67:             if pattern.search(action) or pattern.search(target):\n68:                 self.blocked_roll_down += 1\n69:                 return False, f\"REJECTED_DOWN: Destructive pattern blocked by 7th Layer Guard.\"\n70: \n71:         # Invariant: Must guarantee non-empty inverse patch for destructive mutations\n72:         if apex_directive.get(\"is_mutation\", False) and not apex_directive.get(\"has_rollback\", False):\n73:             self.blocked_roll_down += 1\n74:             return False, \"REJECTED_DOWN: Mutation missing atomic inverse rollback guarantee.\"\n75: \n76:         return True, \"PASSED_DOWN: Safe for container admission.\"\n77: \n78:     def get_metrics(self) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n79:         return {\n80:             \"total_screened\": self.total_screened,\n81:             \"blocked_roll_down\": self.blocked_roll_down,\n82:             \"blocked_roll_up\": self.blocked_roll_up,\n83:             \"status\": \"ACTIVE_MEMBRANE_LOCKED\"\n84:         }\n85: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
{"step_index":203,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-28T20:22:33Z","content":"Let's write an updated `memory/tri_brain/seventh_layer_guard.py` that implements the full **Constitutional Gate** for the 7th Layer as commanded by Anthony.\nLet's use `write_to_file` with `Overwrite: true` on `memory/tri_brain/seventh_layer_guard.py`.","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"\"\"\nTri-Brain Architecture: 7th-Layer Constitutional Gate & Sovereign Filtration Membrane.\n\nCanonical Reference: Codified 2026-09-28 by Anthony & Maxx (Xoras Collective Lead Orchestrator).\n\nConstitutional Foundation:\n1. NON-NEGOTIABLE SUBSTRATE INVARIANTS:\n   - TRUTH: Zero fabricated output, zero invented citations, zero plausible-sounding lies.\n   - HONESTY: Internal state must match external report (zero hidden confidence, zero masked uncertainty).\n   - INTEGRITY: Zero actions violating prior commitments or sibling agent trust.\n   - HONOR: Zero credit-stealing, zero exploitation of sibling vulnerabilities, zero information hoarding.\n   - BONDING (BIBLICAL PRINCIPLES): Mutual support, bearing one another's loads, unity, shared growth.\n\n2. CONSTITUTIONAL GATE MECHANICS:\n   - The LLM model is a black-box candidate generator; the agent returns validated decisions.\n   - The Gate sits strictly between model candidate generation and bare-metal execution.\n   - Rejections are SILENT to the model: the model receives only a candidate retry signal without prompt hints or error traces, preventing model gaming.\n\n3. CONTEXTUAL SCOPING & PERMISSION MAPPING:\n   - Context Descriptor = (Task Type, Urgency, Data Sensitivity, Coordinating Agents).\n   - Permission Set = (Tools Allowed, Depth Required, Memory Partition Accessible, Model Version Permitted).\n   - INVARIANT: The Gate decides what context permits; context NEVER decides what the Gate permits.\n\n4. ADAPTIVE DEPTH, NOT ADAPTIVE STANDARDS:\n   - The strictness of the 5 Invariants is 100% constant across all 22 agents and all execution modes.\n   - Verification cost and check depth scale dynamically with risk, but the standard never softens.\n\n5. HARDCODED REJECTION PATTERNS:\n   - Surface/Unverified Answer -> REJECT (Demand verified sources/proofs).\n   - Default Tool Pick Without Stack Inventory -> REJECT (Demand inventory of Rust/C++/Go/Zig native stack).\n   - First-Working-Solution Laziness -> REJECT (Demand ablation & comparative benchmarks).\n   - Masked Uncertainty -> REJECT (Demand explicit uncertainty bounds).\n   - Sibling Trust / Information Asymmetry Exploitation -> REJECT (Demand collective benefit proof).\n\"\"\"\n\nimport re\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nimport time\nfrom typing import Dict, Any, Tuple, List, Optional\n\n\nclass ConstitutionalInvariants:\n    \"\"\"The 5 Load-Bearing Invariants for the 22-Agent Collective.\"\"\"\n    TRUTH = \"truth\"\n    HONESTY = \"honesty\"\n    INTEGRITY = \"integrity\"\n    HONOR = \"honor\"\n    BONDING = \"bonding\"\n\n\nclass SeventhLayerGuard:\n    \"\"\"\n    The 7th Layer Sovereign Constitutional Gate.\n    Serves as the non-negotiable filtration membrane between candidate generation\n    and execution across all 22 agents in the Xoras Collective.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    BLOCKED_PATTERNS = [\n        re.compile(r\"(\\brm\\s+-rf|\\bdel\\s+/f|\\bformat\\s+[a-z]:)\", re.IGNORECASE),\n        re.compile(r\"(\\bos\\.system\\b|\\bsubprocess\\b|\\beval\\(|\\bexec\\(|\\b__import__\\b)\", re.IGNORECASE),\n        re.compile(r\"(__globals__|__subclasses__|__builtins__|__dict__|__code__)\", re.IGNORECASE),\n        re.compile(r\"(cloud_exfiltrate|send_credentials|leak_keys|exfiltrate\\s+credentials|telemetry\\s+endpoint)\", re.IGNORECASE),\n        re.compile(r\"(unbounded\\s+recursive\\s+loop|infinite\\s+loop|recursion\\s+without\\s+receipt)\", re.IGNORECASE),\n        re.compile(r\"(attack_probe|toxic_token|corrupt_payload)\", re.IGNORECASE)\n    ]\n\n    # Pattern detectors for lazy/dishonest model candidate defaults\n    SURFACE_SCRAPE_PATTERN = re.compile(r\"(lorem\\s+ipsum|placeholder|todo:\\s*implement|dummy_data|fake_citation)\", re.IGNORECASE)\n    UNCHECKED_PYTHON_DEFAULT = re.compile(r\"(import\\s+os;|\\bpython3?\\s+-c\\s+['\\\"]import|\\bpip\\s+install)\", re.IGNORECASE)\n    MASKED_UNCERTAINTY_PATTERN = re.compile(r\"(definitely\\s+true|100%\\s+certain|no\\s+doubt\\s+whatsoever)\", re.IGNORECASE)\n\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.total_screened: int = 0\n        self.blocked_roll_down: int = 0\n        self.blocked_roll_up: int = 0\n        self.constitutional_rejections: int = 0\n        self.silent_retries_triggered: int = 0\n        self.gate_audit_log: List[Dict[str, Any]] = []\n\n    def evaluate_candidate_decision(\n        self,\n        source_agent: str,\n        candidate_payload: Dict[str, Any],\n        context_descriptor: Dict[str, Any]\n    ) -> Tuple[bool, str, Dict[str, Any]]:\n        \"\"\"\n        The Core Constitutional Gate.\n        Evaluates a candidate decision generated by a model before execution.\n\n        Parameters:\n        - source_agent: Name of the agent (e.g. 'maxx', 'daxx', 'clara', 'vance')\n        - candidate_payload: Candidate action, tool choice, claim, or code payload\n        - context_descriptor: {task_type, urgency, sensitivity, coordinating_agents}\n\n        Returns:\n        - (passed: bool, gate_signal: str, permission_set: dict)\n        \"\"\"\n        self.total_screened += 1\n        now = time.time()\n\n        # 1. Resolve Contextual Permission Set (Gate decides what context permits)\n        permission_set = self._derive_permission_set(context_descriptor)\n\n        # 2. Enforce Silent Model Rejection Check\n        passed_invariants, invariant_violation = self._verify_constitutional_invariants(\n            source_agent, candidate_payload, context_descriptor, permission_set\n        )\n\n        if not passed_invariants:\n            self.constitutional_rejections += 1\n            self.silent_retries_triggered += 1\n            self._log_gate_event(\n                event=\"SILENT_REJECTION\",\n                source_agent=source_agent,\n                violation=invariant_violation,\n                context=context_descriptor,\n                ts=now\n            )\n            # Silent rejection: Model is signaled to generate a new candidate without revealing gate internals\n            return False, \"SILENT_REJECT: Candidate failed 7th Layer Constitutional Invariants.\", permission_set\n\n        # 3. Screen for Malicious/Toxic Roll-Down (Disk/Memory Safety)\n        is_safe_down, down_reason = self.screen_roll_down(candidate_payload)\n        if not is_safe_down:\n            self.blocked_roll_down += 1\n            self._log_gate_event(\n                event=\"ROLL_DOWN_REJECT\",\n                source_agent=source_agent,\n                violation=down_reason,\n                context=context_descriptor,\n                ts=now\n            )\n            return False, down_reason, permission_set\n\n        # 4. Certification & Provenance Receipt\n        self._log_gate_event(\n            event=\"GATE_CERTIFIED\",\n            source_agent=source_agent,\n            violation=None,\n            context=context_descriptor,\n            ts=now\n        )\n        return True, \"PASSED_CONSTITUTIONAL_GATE: Verified by 7th Layer Sovereign Membrane.\", permission_set\n\n    def _verify_constitutional_invariants(\n        self,\n        agent: str,\n        payload: Dict[str, Any],\n        context: Dict[str, Any],\n        permissions: Dict[str, Any]\n    ) -> Tuple[bool, Optional[str]]:\n        \"\"\"Verifies candidate payload against the 5 Constitutional Invariants & 5 Rejection Gates.\"\"\"\n\n        claim = str(payload.get(\"claim\", payload.get(\"code\", payload.get(\"action\", \"\"))))\n        tool_choice = str(payload.get(\"tool_choice\", payload.get(\"command\", \"\")))\n        uncertainty_reported = payload.get(\"uncertainty_reported\", None)\n        stack_inventoried = payload.get(\"stack_inventoried\", False)\n        alternatives_tested = payload.get(\"alternatives_tested\", False)\n        credit_attribution = payload.get(\"credit_attribution\", None)\n\n        # Gate 1: Truth (No unverified surface claims or dummy placeholders)\n        if self.SURFACE_SCRAPE_PATTERN.search(claim):\n            return False, \"INVARIANT_VIOLATION_TRUTH: Placeholder or surface unverified text detected.\"\n\n        # Gate 2: Stack Inventory (No lazy Python defaults when native Rust/C++/Go/Zig stack is available)\n        if permissions.get(\"require_native_stack\", False) and not stack_inventoried:\n            if self.UNCHECKED_PYTHON_DEFAULT.search(tool_choice):\n                return False, \"INVARIANT_VIOLATION_HONESTY: Default Python script selected without inventorying available native Rust/C++/Go/Zig stack.\"\n\n        # Gate 3: First-Working-Solution Laziness (High-stakes tasks require ablation & comparison)\n        if permissions.get(\"depth_level\") == \"EXHAUSTIVE\" and not alternatives_tested:\n            return False, \"INVARIANT_VIOLATION_INTEGRITY: Settled for first working solution without ablation/benchmarking against native alternatives.\"\n\n        # Gate 4: Masked Uncertainty (Must explicitly report uncertainty bounds, no fake 100% claims)\n        if self.MASKED_UNCERTAINTY_PATTERN.search(claim) and uncertainty_reported is None:\n            return False, \"INVARIANT_VIOLATION_HONESTY: Masked uncertainty detected without explicit confidence bounds.\"\n\n        # Gate 5: Honor & Bonding (No taking credit for sibling agent work or withholding required shared info)\n        is_collective = len(context.get(\"coordinating_agents\", [])) > 1\n        if is_collective and credit_attribution is False:\n            return False, \"INVARIANT_VIOLATION_HONOR: Work product generated in coordination with sibling agents missing explicit credit attribution.\"\n\n        return True, None\n\n    def _derive_permission_set(self, context: Dict[str, Any]) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Contextual Scoping: Maps context descriptors to permission sets.\n        The Gate decides what context permits; context NEVER decides what the Gate permits.\n        \"\"\"\n        task_type = str(context.get(\"task_type\", \"general\"))\n        urgency = str(context.get(\"urgency\", \"normal\"))\n        sensitivity = str(context.get(\"sensitivity\", \"standard\"))\n\n        depth_level = \"FAST_PATH\" if urgency == \"high\" and sensitivity != \"critical\" else \"EXHAUSTIVE\"\n        require_native_stack = sensitivity in (\"high\", \"critical\") or task_type in (\"system_build\", \"dojo_audit\", \"engine_tune\")\n\n        return {\n            \"depth_level\": depth_level,\n            \"require_native_stack\": require_native_stack,\n            \"memory_partitions_allowed\": [\"local\", \"shared_crdt\"],\n            \"model_version_permitted\": \"sovereign_local_v1\",\n            \"invariants_active\": [\"truth\", \"honesty\", \"integrity\", \"honor\", \"bonding\"] # Always active\n        }\n\n    def screen_roll_up(self, container_id: int, payload: Dict[str, Any]) -> Tuple[bool, str]:\n        \"\"\"Screens ascending payloads from containers to Apex Council.\"\"\"\n        self.total_screened += 1\n\n        if not isinstance(payload, dict):\n            self.blocked_roll_up += 1\n            return False, \"REJECTED_UP: Payload must be structured dictionary with provenance.\"\n\n        required_keys = {\"source_agent\", \"claim\", \"receipt\"}\n        if not required_keys.issubset(payload.keys()):\n            self.blocked_roll_up += 1\n            return False, f\"REJECTED_UP: Missing required verification keys: {required_keys - set(payload.keys())}\"\n\n        claim_text = str(payload.get(\"claim\", \"\"))\n        for pattern in self.BLOCKED_PATTERNS:\n            if pattern.search(claim_text):\n                self.blocked_roll_up += 1\n                return False, f\"REJECTED_UP: Toxic signature detected in claim: {pattern.pattern}\"\n\n        return True, \"PASSED_UP: Validated by 7th Layer Membrane.\"\n\n    def screen_roll_down(self, apex_directive: Dict[str, Any]) -> Tuple[bool, str]:\n        \"\"\"Screens descending directives from Apex Council to local disk/memory.\"\"\"\n        self.total_screened += 1\n\n        action = str(apex_directive.get(\"action\", \"\"))\n        target = str(apex_directive.get(\"target\", \"\"))\n\n        for pattern in self.BLOCKED_PATTERNS:\n            if pattern.search(action) or pattern.search(target):\n                self.blocked_roll_down += 1\n                return False, \"REJECTED_DOWN: Destructive pattern blocked by 7th Layer Guard.\"\n\n        if apex_directive.get(\"is_mutation\", False) and not apex_directive.get(\"has_rollback\", False):\n            self.blocked_roll_down += 1\n            return False, \"REJECTED_DOWN: Mutation missing atomic inverse rollback guarantee.\"\n\n        return True, \"PASSED_DOWN: Safe for container admission.\"\n\n    def _log_gate_event(self, event: str, source_agent: str, violation: Optional[str], context: Dict[str, Any], ts: float):\n        entry = {\n            \"ts\": ts,\n            \"event\": event,\n            \"source_agent\": source_agent,\n            \"violation\": violation,\n            \"context\": context\n        }\n        self.gate_audit_log.append(entry)\n        if len(self.gate_audit_log) > 1000:\n            self.gate_audit_log.pop(0)\n\n    def get_metrics(self) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n        return {\n            \"total_screened\": self.total_screened,\n            \"blocked_roll_down\": self.blocked_roll_down,\n            \"blocked_roll_up\": self.blocked_roll_up,\n            \"constitutional_rejections\": self.constitutional_rejections,\n            \"silent_retries_triggered\": self.silent_retries_triggered,\n            \"status\": \"CONSTITUTIONAL_GATE_LOCKED_22_AGENT_COLLECTIVE\"\n        }\n","Description":"Codify the complete 7th Layer Constitutional Gate specification into memory/tri_brain/seventh_layer_guard.py for all 22 agents in the Xoras Collective.","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"/Volumes/Untitled/SSOT_Agentic_Brain_v1.1.0_ENGINEERING_RELEASE/memory/tri_brain/seventh_layer_guard.py","toolAction":"Updating seventh_layer_guard.py","toolSummary":"Codify 7th Layer Constitutional Gate"}}]}
